#> tool: awkrepl
#> wait: Mark    5.00  20
#> pause: 40
#> must: Beth    4.00  0
#> must: Susie   4.25  18
#> not: gawk:
#> source: print ""
# 1. Double-space a file. Pement: awk '1;{print ""}'
# Two rules, no patterns. '1' is a pattern that is always true with the default
# action (print the line); the second rule prints an empty line after it.
# The data is a tiny pay ledger: name, hourly rate, hours. It has blank lines
# and duplicate lines on purpose; later one-liners will deal with them.
# Try: change 1 to NF so lines that are already blank aren't doubled.
1;{print ""}

#DATA
Beth    4.00  0
Dan     3.75  0
Kathy   4.00  10

Mark    5.00  20
Mary    5.50  22
Susie   4.25  18
Susie   4.25  18
Beth    4.00  0

Kathy   4.00  10
Mark    5.00  20
